.TH BETTERGUAC-SYNC 8 "November 2026" "betterguac" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
betterguac-sync \- apply a BetterGuac YAML file to the database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B betterguac-sync
.RB plan
.I file.yaml
.br
.B betterguac-sync
.RB apply
.I file.yaml
.B \-\-confirm
.I plan-id
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads servers, groups and users from a YAML file, shows a preview of what
would change, and applies a previewed plan by its ID. It only changes
objects it created itself and never touches protected accounts. Run
.B betterguac-sync \-\-help
for every command.
.SH FILES
/etc/betterguac/betterguac.yaml (starter file),
/usr/share/betterguac/betterguac.yaml.example (full example),
/etc/betterguac/sync.env (database login, root only)
